{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user provided a detailed stitch task (ID 5165) to implement srd018-head requirements R1.5, R2.1, R2.2, R2.3 for the `cmd/head` utility in the go-unix-utils project. Specifically:\n   - R1.5: Ensure line termination semantics (newline-terminated, last line without newline still counted)\n   - R2.1: Add `-c NUM` / `--bytes=NUM` byte-count mode, mutually exclusive with `-n` (last flag wins)\n   - R2.2: Support negative byte counts (`-c -100`) that print all bytes except the last NUM\n   - R2.3: Support multiplier suffixes on byte counts: b(512), K/KiB(1024), M/MiB(1048576), G/GiB(1073741824)\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/head/main.go` and `cmd/head/head_test.go`. Acceptance criteria require `go build`, `go vet`, and `go test` all passing.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` against `ghead` (GNU head from Homebrew)\n   - `pkg/sizeparse` package for parsing size strings with multiplier suffixes\n   - `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` for SIGPIPE handling (already in place)\n   - `countMode` type enum with `modeLines` and `modeBytes` (modeBytes already defined but unused)\n   - Negative counts mean \"all except last N\" for both lines and bytes\n   - LC_ALL=C environment for tests per project convention\n   - The `DiffTest` struct: `{ Name string; Args []string; Stdin []byte; Env []string; WorkDir string; ExitCode int; ... }`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd018-head.yaml** (READ - full SRD)\n     - Defines all requirements R1.1-R1.5, R2.1-R2.3, R3.1-R3.5, R4.1-R4.4\n     - Non-goals: no -z (NUL delimiter), no decimal suffixes (kB/MB/GB), no file following\n     - Package contract imports: `pkg/sizeparse` and `pkg/sys`\n   \n   - **cmd/head/main.go** (READ - 249 lines, needs modification)\n     - Current state implements R1.1-R1.4 only (line mode)\n     - Key existing code:\n     ```go\n     type countMode int\n     const (\n         modeLines countMode = iota\n         modeBytes\n     )\n     type options struct {\n         mode  countMode\n         count int64\n     }\n     ```\n     - `parseShortFlags` only handles `'n'` - needs `'c'`, `'q'`, `'v'` added (though q/v are R3.x, not in scope unless needed for tests)\n     - `parseLongFlag` only handles `--lines`, `--help`, `--version` - needs `--bytes`, and possibly `--quiet`/`--silent`/`--verbose`\n     - `processFile` always calls `headLines` regardless of `opts.mode` - needs to dispatch to `headBytes` for `modeBytes`\n     - `parseLineCount` uses simple `strconv.ParseInt` - byte count parsing needs `sizeparse` for suffix support\n     - `headLinesFromStart` and `headLinesFromEnd` exist and work correctly\n     - No `headBytes`, `headBytesFromStart`, or `headBytesFromEnd` functions exist yet\n   \n   - **cmd/head/head_test.go** (NOT YET READ - needs to be read before modification)\n   \n   - **pkg/sizeparse/parse.go** (provided in project_context source_code)\n     - `Parse(s string) (int64, error)` - basic parsing\n     - `ParseWithOptions(s string, opts ParseOptions) (int64, error)` - with sign support\n     - `ParseOptions{AllowSign bool; DefaultUnit int64}`\n     - Supports suffixes: b(512), K/KiB(1024), KB(1000), M/MiB, MB, G/GiB, GB, T/TiB, etc.\n   \n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (contract provided, not read)\n     - `DiffTest` struct, `RunDiffTests`, `BuildBinary` - used for differential testing\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - was still in the reading/planning phase when interrupted.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand exact requirements\n   - Read existing main.go to understand what's already implemented and what needs to be added\n   - Identif