arseLongFlag`\n   - Add `parseByteCount(s string) (int64, error)` that uses `sizeparse.ParseWithOptions` with `AllowSign: true`\n   - Add `headBytes(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, count int64) error` dispatcher\n   - Add `headBytesFromStart(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, n int64) error` using `io.CopyN`\n   - Add `headBytesFromEnd(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, n int64) error` that buffers all input and writes all except last n bytes\n   - Update `processFile` to check `opts.mode` and call either `headLines` or `headBytes`\n   - Optionally add `-q`/`-v` flag parsing if needed for test completeness (though R3.x is not in scope)\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Read `cmd/head/head_test.go` to see the existing test structure, then implement all changes to both `cmd/head/main.go` and `cmd/head/head_test.go` in a single pass before building/testing. The task description states: \"requirements: R1 (R1.5), R2 (R2.1), R3 (R2.2), R4 (R2.3)\" and \"files: cmd/head/main.go (modify), cmd/head/head_test.go (modify)\". The acceptance criteria require: \"go build ./cmd/head/ succeeds\", \"go vet ./cmd/head/ reports no issues\", \"go test ./cmd/head/... -count=1 passes\".\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5165/da4faa5c-0f1e-406c-be26-9d1ebc8f2b9c.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da4faa5c-0f1e-406c-be26-9d1ebc8f2b9c","uuid":"ecc81ce0-65b0-4c66-84b0-951bc86519f7","timestamp":"2026-05-14T12:54:21.410Z","isSynthetic":true}
